# tests/recursion/framebuffer.rxt -- [DD-14.FB] (D71 item 2, D73), the
# caller-provided frame buffer, as corpus cells.
#
# WHAT MAKES THIS A CORPUS FILE RATHER THAN A C DRIVER. Every cell below is
# ONE artifact answering ONE subject; the only thing that varies between them
# is WHICH ENTRY was called and, where a buffer is supplied, how big it was.
# `frames-buffer=` (docs/testing.md) is positional within the block, so the
# give-up and the match sit in the same block, compiled once, and cannot
# differ by an accident of two compiles.
#
# THE PATTERN. `^(a(?1)?b)$` is the ruling's own worked specimen: a recursion
# whose depth grows with the subject, so the frame capacity is a SUBJECT SIZE
# rather than a number. MEASURED at the stamped 2048/3072: the largest
# matching n is 512, a 1,024-byte subject, and n = 513 gives up (design §7.1
# measured 342/343 before K134's trail compaction).
#
# WHY THE TRAIL PER LEVEL MATTERS TO THE CELLS BELOW. Design §4 MEASURED
# 2.000 resume frames and 8.982 trail entries per nesting level. Since K134's
# trail compaction (lane trailgc, 2026-10-29) about 3 of those 9 stay live per
# level, and a compaction succeeds only if it leaves the trail at most half
# full, so the trail still binds first at the stamped defaults: the largest
# matching n moved from 342 to 512, and n = 513 needs 1,026 frames (of 2,048)
# and 3,075 trail entries (of 3,072). That is why the descriptor carries both arrays and
# why the capacities below are deliberately ASYMMETRIC: a route that could
# only set them equal could not tell a correct build from one that passed the
# frame capacity as the trail capacity (sabotage row S-FB2).

pattern ^(a(?1)?b)$
features recursion
engine vm

# 1. THE DEFAULT ENTRY, at the give-up boundary's two sides. n = 512 matches;
#    n = 513 is PCREC_ERR_FRAMES. This half is D73's ruling made checkable:
#    the stamped default STAYS 2048/3072, so this give-up is the shipped
#    behaviour and not a defect -- what changes is that a caller now has a way
#    around it.
m "" 0 1024
gu frames ""

# 2. THE SAME SUBJECT THROUGH `<prefix>_search_in` WITH A LARGER BUFFER, in
#    THIS SAME BLOCK, off THIS SAME artifact. This is the feature: the stamped
#    number is a DEFAULT, not a limit.
#
#    2048 FRAMES AND 8192 TRAIL, AND THE ASYMMETRY IS THE POINT. n = 513 needs
#    1,026 frames and 3,075 trail entries, so both capacities are sufficient as
#    written -- and INSUFFICIENT IF SWAPPED (2,048 trail entries against 3,075
#    needed; measured: 8192,2048 gives up). A build that passed `nframes` as the trail capacity therefore
#    fails this cell instead of passing it, which is exactly what a pair of
#    equal capacities could not detect.
frames-buffer=2048,8192
m "" 0 1026

# 3. THE TRAIL IS THE ARRAY THAT BINDS, pinned rather than asserted. Design §4
#    MEASURED it: with the resume capacity raised to 200,000 and the trail left
#    at its stamped 3,072, the give-up n is STILL the default's (513 since
#    K134's compaction; 343 when measured). So a frames-only version
#    of this feature would have bought this caller literally nothing, and this
#    cell is what would go red if the trail ever stopped being caller-provided.
frames-buffer=200000,3072
gu frames ""

# 4. AND THE FRAMES CAN BIND TOO, which is what stops cell 3 from being read as
#    "the trail is the only real capacity". 512 frames is below the 1,026 this
#    subject needs, with the trail far above binding.
#
#    MEASURED AFTERWARDS, AND IT IS A BETTER REASON THAN THE ONE ABOVE: this
#    is the ONLY cell in this file that detects sabotage row S179 (the `_in`
#    entry binding the STAMPED capacity instead of the caller's `nframes`).
#    Cell 2 cannot -- pinning the resume capacity at 2048 hands that cell MORE
#    frames than the 1024 it asked for, so it still matches -- and cells 1, 3,
#    5 and 6 do not vary the resume capacity downward at all. A cell written
#    for symmetry turned out to be the single detector for the most plausible
#    way to build this feature and have it look finished.
frames-buffer=512,400000
gu frames ""

# 5. THE NULL DESCRIPTOR IS THE UN-SUFFIXED CALL (spec §10.3), on both sides of
#    the boundary. Not "equivalent in observable behaviour" -- the same call,
#    which is why these two cells repeat cell 1's expectations verbatim and
#    must keep repeating them. The delegation running the other way round
#    (`_in` owning the default storage) would still pass these; what it would
#    lose is the stack frame, which tests/thread's case measures instead.
frames-buffer=null
m "" 0 1024
gu frames ""

# 6. BACK TO THE DEFAULT ROUTE, so the file also pins that `frames-buffer=` is
#    positional and reversible rather than a one-way switch for the rest of the
#    block. A cell after this line must behave exactly as cell 1 did.
frames-buffer=default
m "" 0 1024

# A SECOND PATTERN, to pin that the route resets with the block. This one is
# not call-bearing at all: `(a|aa)+b` is the unbounded-but-call-free class
# design §3 MEASURES at 98 KB of stack, and it takes the caller-buffer surface
# for the same reason -- the feature is emitted on every VM artifact rather
# than gated on `has_calls`, because trail exhaustion is not a recursion-
# specific failure (design §10).
pattern (a|aa)+b
engine vm
m "aaab" 0 4
frames-buffer=null
m "aaab" 0 4
frames-buffer=64,64
m "aaab" 0 4
n "aaac"

# A DFA-SELECTED PATTERN THROUGH THE SAME ROUTES. The whole surface is emitted
# on a DFA artifact too, INERT (spec §10.4): `<prefix>_search_in` exists, takes
# a descriptor and ignores it, and the sizing macros read 0. So one caller call
# site compiles and answers identically whichever engine the pattern selected
# -- which is the property §6.3's own closing warning asks for, and it is
# checkable only by running the same cells through both engines.
pattern a(b|c)+d
m "abcd" 0 4
frames-buffer=null
m "abcd" 0 4
frames-buffer=4096,4096
m "abcd" 0 4
n "abce"
